## III. The people

### mac-miller
Malcolm McCormick died on 7 September 2018 of counterfeit oxycodone pills containing fentanyl. Cameron Pettit sold them to him; Ryan Reavis supplied Pettit at Stephen Walter's direction. Walter received more than 17 years and Reavis 131 months. His mother, Karen Meyers, told the court that her life "went dark" when he died. His last album, *Circles*, was released posthumously in 2020.
**links:** fentanyl · oxycodone · drug-checking (a test strip reads that pill) · prohibition (a regulated supply does not hide fentanyl in an oxycodone pill).

### juice-wrld
Jarad Higgins died on 8 December 2019, aged 21, of an accidental overdose of oxycodone and codeine. His music was about opioids and his own addiction.
**links:** oxycodone · purdue-pharma (the prescription-opioid culture his generation grew up in).

### kanye-west
He has described becoming dependent on opioids after liposuction in 2016, a dependence that came before his hospitalisation that year. He has spoken publicly about his bipolar diagnosis.
**links:** oxycodone · the-medical-system (a prescription as the route into dependence).

### keltner
Dacher Keltner (Berkeley; Greater Good Science Center; Berkeley Social Interaction Lab) studies compassion, awe and the science of happiness. Avik studied with him. Keltner calls compassion the emotion most people believe is the most important. His *Awe* (2023) defines awe as the emotion of encountering vast mysteries we don't understand. In his review with Monroy, "Awe as a Pathway to Mental and Physical Health", awe works through reduced self-focus, more prosocial relating, social integration and meaning-making. He is part of the Berkeley Center for the Science of Psychedelics (co-founded 2020 by Michael Pollan) and calls awe "one of the key ingredients of psychedelics".
**links:** psilocybin (self-transcendence) · compassion · 5-HT2A (default-mode network) · the-thesis (happiness as the measure of what a society ending this suffering would be).

